Title: F1-M01 — Ashes at First Light (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

> FADE IN:

INT. FORWARD COMMAND POST - DAWN

[[AMBIENCE: radio hiss, distant engines, wind against canvas]]
[[MUSIC: restrained military tension]]

A map of the border farmland is spread across a trestle table. CAPTAIN ELIAN and MIRA stand over it.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(serious)
The relay went dark at 04:10. By dawn, every unit north of the ridge was operating on stale orders.

MIRA
(dry)
Operating on nothing, Captain. The garrison has not acknowledged a message since the relay stopped.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: farmland south-west start, ore ridge to the north, road junction at centre, eastern road fading into unlit hills]]

MIRA
(measured)
Scouts report a small hostile camp around the junction. No heavy armour yet.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(firm)
Then we move before they can reinforce it. Establish a base, secure the junction, and keep the relay road open.

MIRA
(analytical)
We have one construction yard and five rifles. Power first, then barracks, or we are a camp ourselves.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(pointing at map)
The ore is on the ridge. Get a harvester working before the fight starts, not during it.

MIRA
(concerned)
One thing I cannot explain. The camp sits on a junction that has no value unless someone knew we were coming here.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(neutral)
Note it. Take the junction and we will read what they left behind.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

> FADE OUT.
